<p>NOTE: In August 1996 Laserscope acquired Heraeus Surgical Inc. in a transaction which was accounted for using the purchase method. In the quarter ended Sept. 30, 1996, the company expensed $2.4 million of the purchase price related to in-process research and development and also wrote off $0.9 million of Laserscope's inventory and fixed assets which became redundant after the acquisition.  Excluding these non-recurring charges, the company's net income per share would have been $0.17 for the twelve months ended Dec. 31, 1996.</p>
